                "name": "bxmo-2011-1",
                "statement": "An ordered pair of integers $(m, n)$ with $1 < m < n$ is said to be a Benelux couple if the following two conditions hold: $m$ has the same prime divisors as $n$, and $m + {k}$ has the same prime divisors as $n + {k_squared}$.\n\nFind {l} Benelux couples $(m, n)$ with $m \\leqslant {max_val}$ such that for any two pairs $(m_1, n_1), (m_2, n_2)$ with $n_1 > n_2$ in your list, $\\frac{{n_1}}{{n_2}} \\geqslant 4$.",
